1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:01,789
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:05,449
In this lesson, we will build a roster dispatch can use.

3
00:00:05,889 --> 00:00:09,550
An out-of-date roster leaves dispatchers guessing which station,

4
00:00:09,579 --> 00:00:11,869
team, or role a member belongs to.

5
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:15,699
We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:15,699 --> 00:00:17,600
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:18,159 --> 00:00:21,800
A volunteer department creates Station 1 and Station 2 groups,

8
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:26,099
invites 24 members and assigns Engineer and Firefighter roles.

9
00:00:26,470 --> 00:00:31,169
Dispatch, notifications, permissions and reports all start from who belongs

10
00:00:31,169 --> 00:00:33,650
to which group, so set this up first.

11
00:00:34,029 --> 00:00:37,660
The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:39,859
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:40,419 --> 00:00:41,160
Personnel.

14
00:00:41,599 --> 00:00:44,519
Member accounts, contact details and status.

15
00:00:44,970 --> 00:00:48,649
Invite members or add them directly, then check that each has

16
00:00:48,649 --> 00:00:50,560
a mobile number or email address.

17
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:52,289
Manage Invites.

18
00:00:52,730 --> 00:00:55,769
Email invitations for new members to join the department.

19
00:00:56,189 --> 00:01:00,019
Send invitations and follow up on any that have not been accepted.

20
00:01:00,679 --> 00:01:02,029
Groups & Stations.

21
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:05,460
Stations and groups that organize members and units.

22
00:01:05,869 --> 00:01:10,230
Create a station group for each station with its address, and organizational

23
00:01:10,230 --> 00:01:12,959
groups for teams, then add members.

24
00:01:13,690 --> 00:01:14,800
Personnel roles.

25
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:18,809
Roles such as Firefighter, EMT or Officer.

26
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:23,150
Create the roles you dispatch or report on, and assign them to members.

27
00:01:23,769 --> 00:01:24,679
Add Person.

28
00:01:25,139 --> 00:01:28,689
Create a member account directly instead of sending an invitation.

29
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:33,059
Have your member list with email addresses or mobile numbers, and decide

30
00:01:33,059 --> 00:01:35,120
how stations or teams are grouped.

31
00:01:35,739 --> 00:01:36,339
New Group.

32
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:38,340
Create a station or group.

33
00:01:38,809 --> 00:01:42,559
Have your member list with email addresses or mobile numbers, and decide

34
00:01:42,559 --> 00:01:44,590
how stations or teams are grouped.

35
00:01:45,119 --> 00:01:47,879
For the training scenario, work in this order.

36
00:01:48,350 --> 00:01:48,869
Step 1.

37
00:01:49,449 --> 00:01:52,819
Create Station 1 and Station 2 with their addresses.

38
00:01:53,260 --> 00:01:54,029
Step 2.

39
00:01:54,479 --> 00:01:57,359
Invite sample members and assign their station groups.

40
00:01:57,790 --> 00:01:58,519
Step 3.

41
00:01:58,939 --> 00:02:02,619
Create Engineer and Officer roles and assign them deliberately.

42
00:02:03,209 --> 00:02:04,740
Now verify the result.

43
00:02:05,209 --> 00:02:08,680
Verify a sample member appears in the correct group and role.

44
00:02:09,119 --> 00:02:12,470
Check an accepted invitation and the member contact details.

45
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:17,720
A common problem to watch for: An invitation is not an accepted membership.

46
00:02:18,230 --> 00:02:21,450
A role label is not proof of a current certification.

47
00:02:21,899 --> 00:02:23,430
Review both separately.

48
00:02:24,079 --> 00:02:25,640
Your practice task is simple.

49
00:02:26,079 --> 00:02:31,000
Invite one sample member, assign a station and role, and have that member sign in.

50
00:02:31,429 --> 00:02:33,459
Track unaccepted invitations.

51
00:02:33,790 --> 00:02:37,620
Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

